[{:seon.task/name "spit-writes-through-what-is-not-a-regular-file"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-26 (seon.check-test's lock test hung 1 h 45): Jolt's spit to a FIFO returned at once and replaced the FIFO with a regular file holding the text (ls: prw-r--r-- before, -rw-r--r-- after), and a reader that had opened the FIFO waited for good. Cause: host/chez/java/io.ss jolt-spit writes a non-append spit to a temp file in the same directory and renames it over the target (so a failed write never truncates), which replaces whatever node the path names: a FIFO, a device, and a symlink (the link itself, where the JVM writes its target). JVM Clojure's spit opens a FileOutputStream on the path, which writes through a FIFO (blocking until a reader opens), a device, and a symlink's target. Correct, at the cause: the temp-and-rename write is for a regular file or a new one; a path that exists and is not a regular file, or is a symlink, is opened and written through, as the JVM does. Proof red first, a corpus row from JVM values: a FIFO read by a child process (ProcessBuilder cat) receives what spit wrote and is still a FIFO after; a symlink to a file still is one and its target holds the text."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
 {:seon.task/name "empty-of-a-queue-is-a-queue"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-30 (seon.agent/take-op's test): Jolt's (empty clojure.lang.PersistentQueue/EMPTY) and (empty q) of a non-empty queue answer clojure.lang.PersistentList$EmptyList, where Clojure answers PersistentQueue/EMPTY (clojure.lang.PersistentQueue.empty()). So (into (empty q) xs) conses to the front and reverses the order, silently: [3 4] into a queue's empty read back [4 3]. Correct: empty of a PersistentQueue is PersistentQueue/EMPTY with the queue's meta, as the reference's IPersistentCollection.empty does. Fixed in Jolt, on a jolt/ branch of seantempesta/jolt, with a unit case beside empty's other collection cases; Seon's take-op builds on PersistentQueue/EMPTY meanwhile and may then use (empty q)."
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}]
